IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA (pre-repair):\n\nStep 0 dossier:\n- Step 0(a): duplicate/history sweep for `anthropic httpx2 http_client rejects AsyncClient` found this bug (2bd6) and its stopgap predecessor 1f35; no separate open duplicate was identified in the targeted search. `rebar list --type bug --status open,in_progress` was run for the required open-bug sweep.\n- Step 0(b): no report build quoted in this ticket; using created_at=1788111163572289990 gives floor 580125bf3ff65003a063c3358a50d12f0a3b99a4. Suspect paths changed since (notably 254e jitter/backoff and 1f35 cap commits).\n- Step 0(c): fresh worktree debug-2bd6-httpx2 is current at 1d9193332139894cc46f5e7385e070d8bd06d5a2 (= origin/main).\n\nConfirmed mechanism: with anthropic 1.2.0 installed, `AsyncAnthropic.__init__` annotates `http_client: httpx2.AsyncClient | None`, while `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py:212-215` still constructs a stdlib `httpx.AsyncClient` and passes it as `http_client`. Runtime reproduction in the fresh worktree raises exactly: `TypeError: Invalid http_client argument; Expected an instance of httpx2.AsyncClient but got <class 'httpx.AsyncClient'>` from `anthropic/_client.py:692` when `_build_retrying_anthropic_provider()` reaches `anthropic_model.py:214`.\n\nLegitimacy: incomplete-implementation/defect under this ticket's approved Decision 6 scope and 1f35's stopgap: 1f35 documents that the `<1` SDK cap only keeps mirror-sweep legs off the httpx2 line until this seam is adapted; 2bd6 explicitly approves adapting the seam and lifting/widening the cap while preserving 254e Retry-After+jitter semantics.\n\nAttribution: env-integration escape attributed to `morbid-uncultured-arcticduck` / 95a5-41eb-cffd-477b by scope and commit evidence. Commit 434dc0a5779f164a082cd688783d71024fd93837 (rebar-ticket: morbid-uncultured-arcticduck) introduced the transport-layer retry seam and the custom `httpx.AsyncClient` passed to Anthropic with SDK retries disabled. Later 254e (5c28ce66...) only hardened wait semantics and 1f35 (cd40322e...) was the temporary cap, not the origin. The external anthropic 1.x/httpx2 contract created the obligation, but the rebar work item that owned this custom-client integration is 95a5/morbid.\n\nPlanned repair: preserve the existing stdlib-httpx path for pre-httpx2 SDKs, detect SDKs whose `http_client` contract names `httpx2.AsyncClient`, build an equivalent httpx2 client/transport with the same tenacity retry predicate, wait strategy, SDK `max_retries=0`, timeout, teardown, and Retry-After/jitter semantics, then lift the 1f35 direct upper bound.","timestamp":1788225588786757001}],"created_at":1788111163572289990,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"90801151-20df-48ad-8bba-7e027aff0362","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1f35-74fc-47a0-4d71"},{"link_uuid":"de103d67-8258-4970-b2f1-e7cab17c1350","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"eb64-844b-ab7a-4915"},{"link_uuid":"77411405-5cb6-439b-8792-600bca12c577","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"95a5-41eb-cffd-477b"},{"link_uuid":"83b4d15e-8ebd-4b07-8599-8969deb7ac18","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d33a-8fd4-afcb-4ff8"},{"link_uuid":"a6f31cd9-238c-4ca7-966e-9c2b213376e0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ef38-be67-9c6b-47b2"},{"link_uuid":"802f5e99-080b-481e-b537-14897ba2d764","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3463-c953-693c-4801"}],"description":"## Context\n\nSplit from `floating-chromium-leafwing` (1f35-74fc-47a0-4d71), Decision 6 (operator-approved 2026-08-30). 1f35 was the stopgap: bound `anthropic` below the first httpx2-vendoring release (`<1`) so mirror-sweep legs stopped floating to SDKs whose `http_client` contract rejects a stdlib `httpx.AsyncClient`. The dependency boundary is `1.0.0`: `anthropic` 1.x (including the reproduced `1.2.0`) declares and validates `httpx2`, while `0.121.0` remains the pre-httpx2 line. This ticket is the approved long-term fix: adapt rebar's Anthropic provider seam for both contracts and widen the temporary cap.\n\n## Why this followed eb64 / 254e\n\nThe changed seam is `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py:_build_retrying_anthropic_provider`, inside epic `financial-stoneware-brant` (eb64-844b-ab7a-4915) and overlapping 254e. 254e's invariant is transport-owned retry: rebar supplies the HTTP client, sets `AsyncAnthropic(max_retries=0)`, retries transient 429/529/5xx plus timeout/network errors below the agent loop, honors positive `Retry-After`, and falls back to jitter. This fix preserves that invariant; it does not switch to SDK-managed retries.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Choose the type-detected custom-client branch because it is the branch compatible with 254e's `max_retries=0` transport-owned retry invariant.\n- Detect the SDK contract by reading `inspect.signature(AsyncAnthropic.__init__).parameters[\"http_client\"].annotation`; if its text contains `httpx2.AsyncClient`, select `httpx2`, otherwise default to stdlib `httpx` when the annotation is absent or ambiguous.\n- Build one shared `RetryConfig` and one shared `_validate_response` against the selected module. The retry predicate uses the selected module's `HTTPStatusError`, `TimeoutException`, and `NetworkError`; `_build_retry_wait` reads `exc.response.headers` generically, so the same Retry-After/jitter rules apply to both exception families.\n- For stdlib `httpx`, keep pydantic-ai's existing `AsyncTenacityTransport`. For `httpx2`, first check for a first-party `pydantic_ai.retries.HTTPX2TenacityTransport`; the current pinned pydantic-ai lacks it, so this patch uses a local `httpx2.AsyncBaseTransport` wrapper with the same retry/validate/close/context-manager behavior.\n- Handle Anthropic 1.x beta `messages.create` signature removal by wrapping the rebar-owned `anthropic_client.beta.messages.create` instance after provider construction. The wrapper moves unsupported real sampling kwargs (`temperature`, `top_p`, `top_k`) into `extra_body` and only drops `anthropic.Omit` placeholders. Upstream capability resolution still decides whether a model gets a real sampling value; the wrapper only changes the Python-call location required by the SDK signature. Provider-parity normalization continues to read the final wire JSON, where `extra_body` is merged into the top-level request body.\n- Widen `anthropic` to `>=0.121.0,<2`, keeping both pre-httpx2 and 1.x/httpx2 lines installable while excluding the next major line.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `anthropic==1.2.0`: provider/model construction uses `httpx2.AsyncClient`, does not raise the old `TypeError`, and can issue a MockTransport request through `AnthropicProvider`/`AnthropicModel`.\n- [ ] `anthropic==0.121.0`: provider/model construction remains compatible with stdlib `httpx.AsyncClient`.\n- [ ] 254e retry semantics are preserved for the selected HTTP module: retry predicate, Retry-After parsing, zero/expired-header fallback, jitter wait, and `max_retries=0` guard.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_transport_retry.py` covers httpx2 construction, retry, and sampling-kwarg relocation.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_transport_retry_jitter.py` remains green for `_build_retry_wait`'s shared Retry-After/jitter contract.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py` captures direct-Anthropic requests through the SDK-selected transport module and confirms sampling values remain visible in the normalized wire payload.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py`, `tests/unit/test_agentic_message_cache.py`, `tests/unit/test_llm_provider_factory.py`, and `tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py` are updated for the SDK-selected client contract.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_packaging_dependencies.py` proves `0.121.0` and `1.2.0` are allowed while `2.0.0` is rejected.\n- [ ] Portable across CI providers / no CI: the adaptation is local Python plus dependency bounds; no provider-specific CI trigger is required.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py","reason":"Adapt Anthropic provider/client construction seam for SDKs whose http_client contract is httpx2 while preserving transport retry semantics."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_transport_retry.py","reason":"Add/adjust provider retry tests covering httpx2 construction, retry/backoff behavior, and sampling kwargs moved through extra_body under Anthropic 1.x."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_transport_retry_jitter.py","reason":"Existing shared _build_retry_wait Retry-After/jitter contract must remain green after generic exception/header parsing."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_packaging_dependencies.py","reason":"Update dependency-spec regression test from temporary cap to post-fix widened/lifted bound."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_provider_factory.py","reason":"Update Anthropic provider factory seam tests to patch the SDK's selected stdlib-httpx or httpx2 transport and verify lifecycle/closure."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py","reason":"Update Anthropic timeout tests to expect the SDK-selected http client exception type."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py","reason":"Update fallback-chain tests to observe retrying clients under either stdlib-httpx or httpx2 contracts."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_agentic_message_cache.py","reason":"Update message-cache capture harness to use the SDK-selected http client module under the httpx2 contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py","reason":"Update provider-parity capture harness to intercept the SDK-selected Anthropic transport and preserve sampling-payload parity under httpx2."},{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"Widen the temporary anthropic<1 cap introduced by 1f35 once the seam supports httpx2 while retaining a <2 major ceiling."},{"path":"uv.lock","reaso